.TH ICED\-LIBADWAITA\-DESKTOP.CONF 5 "2026-11-03" "iced-libadwaita 0.1.0" "iced-libadwaita Manual"
.SH NAME
desktop.conf \- the shared desktop configuration of iced\-libadwaita applications
.SH DESCRIPTION
Desktop\-level behavior is defined \fIonce per desktop\fR, in a shared file, so every iced\-libadwaita application behaves the same way. Applications read these decisions; they do not hard\-code them.
.PP
The file is in the GLib key\-file format: \fB[section]\fR headers, \fBkey=value\fR lines and \fB#\fR comments. Every setting is optional; the values shown below are the defaults. Invalid or unknown values are ignored with a warning.
.SH FILES
Lowest to highest priority:
.IP 1. 3
the built\-in defaults (the HIG defaults);
.IP 2. 3
system files, \fI$XDG_CONFIG_DIRS/iced\-libadwaita/desktop.conf\fR (default \fI/etc/xdg\fR);
.IP 3. 3
the user file, \fI$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/iced\-libadwaita/desktop.conf\fR (default \fI~/.config\fR);
.IP 4. 3
the application's opt\-outs, if \fBpolicy.allow\-app\-overrides\fR allows them.
.PP
Later files win per key. \fBICED_LIBADWAITA_CONFIG\fR=\fIpath\fR replaces files 2 and 3 with one file.
.SH SETTINGS
.SS [appearance]
.TP
\fBcolor\-scheme\fR=\fIsystem\fR
system | light | dark
.TP
\fBaccent\fR=\fIsystem\fR
system | blue | teal | green | yellow | orange | red | pink | purple | slate
.TP
\fBflat\-headerbars\fR=\fIfalse\fR
header bars with no color of their own (Nautilus\-style)
.TP
\fBauto\-contrast\fR=\fItrue\fR
light/dark text on colored fills by contrast; false = fixed white
.TP
\fBdensity\fR=\fIdefault\fR
default | compact
.TP
\fBtext\-scale\fR=\fI1.0\fR
0.5 .. 3.0
.TP
\fBtransparency\fR=\fI0.0\fR
0 (opaque) .. 1: how see\-through the surfaces are
.TP
\fBtint\fR=\fInone\fR
none | #rrggbb | #rrggbbaa: a color mixed into the surfaces (the alpha is the strength; their own alpha is kept)
.TP
\fBshadows\fR=\fItrue\fR
.TP
\fBshadow\-scale\fR=\fI1.0\fR
.TP
\fBshadow\-intensity\fR=\fI1.0\fR
.SS [motion]
.TP
\fBanimations\fR=\fIsystem\fR
system | on | off
.TP
\fBreduced\-motion\fR=\fIfalse\fR
true: every trigger below is "none" (prefers\-reduced\-motion)
.TP
\fBpage\-change\fR=\fIdefault\fR
content fades in
.TP
\fBpage\-push\fR=\fIdefault\fR
navigation page slides over the previous one
.TP
\fBpopover\fR=\fIdefault\fR
menus and dropdowns rise into place
.TP
\fBselection\fR=\fIdefault\fR
selection highlight fades
.TP
\fBdrawer\fR=\fIdefault\fR
collapsed sidebar slides in over a scrim
.TP
\fBdialog\fR=\fIdefault\fR
dialog scrim + slide
.TP
\fBsheet\fR=\fIdefault\fR
bottom sheet scrim + slide
.TP
\fBtoast\fR=\fIdefault\fR
toast slides up
.TP
\fBreveal\fR=\fIdefault\fR
expanders and banners slide open
.TP
\fBswitch\fR=\fIdefault\fR
switch knob slides
.TP
\fBcarousel\fR=\fIdefault\fR
carousel spring
.TP
\fBlayout\fR=\fIdefault\fR
the sidebar slides in/out of the layout at the collapse breakpoint
.TP
\fBtransition\-close\fR=\fI30\fR
.TP
\fBtransition\-open\fR=\fI30\fR
.SS [windows]
.TP
\fBdecorations\fR=\fIcsd\fR
csd (Adwaita) | ssd (discouraged)
.TP
\fBbutton\-layout\fR=\fIsystem\fR
system | a GTK button\-layout string, e.g. appmenu:close
.TP
\fBmin\-width\fR=\fI360\fR
smallest window
.TP
\fBmin\-height\fR=\fI200\fR
.TP
\fBmobile\-max\-width\fR=\fI575\fR
at or below this width: mobile mode (no window buttons, full\-page menus)
.SS [breakpoints]
.TP
\fBsm\fR=\fI576\fR
.TP
\fBmd\fR=\fI768\fR
.TP
\fBlg\fR=\fI992\fR
.TP
\fBxl\fR=\fI1200\fR
.TP
\fBxxl\fR=\fI1400\fR
.SS [layout]
.TP
\fBpage\-max\-width\fR=\fI600\fR
readable width of pages and preference lists
.SS [navigation]
.TP
\fBcollapse\-width\fR=\fI767\fR
split views collapse at or below this width (just under md = 768)
.TP
\fBmin\-content\-width\fR=\fI520\fR
\&...and whenever the content area would be narrower than this
.TP
\fBsidebar\-fraction\fR=\fI0.25\fR
sidebar width: this share of the window...
.TP
\fBsidebar\-min\-width\fR=\fI180\fR
\&...clamped to min..max
.TP
\fBsidebar\-max\-width\fR=\fI280\fR
.TP
\fBdrawer\-max\-fraction\fR=\fI0.85\fR
a drawer takes at most this share of the window
.TP
\fBmobile\-sidebar\fR=\fIdrawer\fR
drawer | parent\-page
.SS [menus]
.TP
\fBpresentation\fR=\fIauto\fR
auto (full page in mobile mode) | dropdown | full\-page
.SS [shortcuts]
.TP
\fBenabled\fR=\fItrue\fR
keyboard shortcuts work (and are shown)
.TP
\fBhints\fR=\fIauto\fR
auto | always | never: accelerator hints in menus (auto: not in touch menus)
.SS [toasts]
.TP
\fBposition\fR=\fIbottom\-center\fR
top|bottom \- left|center|right, e.g. top\-right
.TP
\fBtarget\fR=\fIcontent\fR
content (content area only, centered on it) | window (over the sidebar too)
.SS [popovers]
.TP
\fBbounds\fR=\fIcontent\fR
content (kept inside the content area it opened from) | window (the whole window)
.SS [rows]
.TP
\fBcollapse\fR=\fIstacked\fR
stacked | flex  (what a wrapped row suffix does)
.TP
\fBwrap\-basis\fR=\fI128\fR
minimum title width before the suffix wraps
.TP
\fBexpander\-indent\fR=\fI24\fR
px a row nested in an expander row is indented (0 = libadwaita's flush nesting)
.SS [icons]
.TP
\fBtheme\fR=\fIsystem\fR
system | an icon theme name
.SS [policy]
.TP
\fBallow\-app\-overrides\fR=\fItrue\fR
.SH EXAMPLES
Compact density with a darker, tinted look:
.PP
.nf
[appearance]
density=compact
color\-scheme=dark
tint=#3584e440
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBiced\-libadwaita\fR(7), \fBiced\-libadwaita\-components\fR(3)
